       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **Typo:** the usual doses are 2.5 mg, 5 mg, or 10 mg once daily. The usual starting dose is 5 mg, or 2.5 mg for frail patients. If you meant 5 mg, I can enter it right away.\n- **Intentional 50 mg:** if this is deliberate, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd also suggest confirming it with pharmacy or the attending first.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
